 "installation": "Steam Quake III Arena, quake3.exe \"Q3 1.32 win-x86 Oct  7 2002\", read only",
 "module": {
  "source": ".tmp/q3-trace/q3trace_module.c (not committed)",
  "abi": "dllEntry/vmMain with Quake III syscall numbers (G_TRACE 24, G_POINT_CONTENTS 25, G_LINKENTITY 30, G_ENTITIES_IN_BOX 32, G_TRACECAPSULE 43); 516-byte sharedEntity_t (entityState_t, then entityShared_t's unused 208-byte entityState_t and its fields), 56-byte trace_t",
  "loading": "retail: Sys_LoadDll (0x447170) tries fs_basepath then fs_cdpath, each with the game directory; the module sits in fs_cdpath/baseq3. fnTech3: fs_homepath/baseq3. Both vm_game 0, sv_pure 0, dedicated 1, developer 1, bot_enable 0",
  "worldBattery": "seeded LCG; four hulls (point, player box, random box up to 32, player box as a capsule trace) x three masks (1, 0x2010001, -1) x three shapes (long, vertical drop, short <=48), 300 of each shape; 1,500 point contents; pass entity 1023",
  "entityBattery": "every brush model *k (up to 32) on entity 300+k, contents 1, moved by (8k,-4k,2k), even k turned (pitch 5*(k%3), yaw 15k); link flags and bounds; 90 traces around each; 200 EntitiesInBox queries; then a player-sized box entity (contents body) traced 300 times with box and capsule hulls"
 },
 "retailFacts": {
  "capsuleEntity": "a trace touching an entity flagged SVF_CAPSULE drops the level: ERROR: CM_ClipHandleToModel: bad handle 1 < 254 < 256; CM_ClipHandleToModel knows no capsule handle. No stock game flags an entity so. fnTech3 traces it as a capsule (inherited) and is not changed to drop.",
  "bevels": "Quake III 1.32 GPL cm_patch.c builds edge bevels in float (VectorSubtract, CrossProduct, DotProduct); fnTech3, from Quake3e through FnQuake3, in double (VectorSubtractDP, CrossProductDP, DotProductDPf), and its brush sweeps use double dot products"
 },
